  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the clear best at 0.485 acc, while scgpt (0.411) and image-only resnet50 (0.208) are substantially weaker. All three completed experiments used singleprofile, so the effect of multiprofile is completely unexplored. Question: Does moving from singleprofile to multiprofile with the best-performing RNA encoder (pca_n2000) improve accuracy? config_002 tests this with the simplest aggregation (avgpool), isolating the profile-setting effect without introducing additional complexity (transformer). This is the best use of experiment 4 because it directly extends our strongest result along one axis, and the answer will inform whether to invest remaining budget in multiprofile variants (transformer, multimodal) or focus on other dimensions like image encoder quality or fusion strategy."
}

